# SPA fallback — required on static hosts (Cloudflare Pages, Netlify).
#
# This is a client-side-routed React Router app: only index.html exists on
# disk, and the router picks the page from the URL once JS boots. Without this
# rule the host looks for a real file at /privacy and returns 404, which would
# break the exact URL Apple requires for the App Store listing, plus /terms,
# /support and every referral link.
#
# 200 (not 301) so the address bar keeps the original path for the router.
/*    /index.html   200
